course: dictionary
lesson: 3754
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence around it shows you which one is meant. The word flush is a good example. «When you flush, a valve opens and water rushes into the bowl» is about cleaning a toilet with water.
explain: Other sentences use flush differently. «Her face flushed» is not about water at all: a face going red from heat, embarrassment or being upset is the meaning. In a building or craft lesson, «flush» means exactly level, so a door that sits flush with the wall is even with it.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. Phrases help too: «flush out» means to make someone or something come out of hiding.
fact: Flush can be a verb, a noun or an adjective, and its job in the sentence shows which one it is.
fact: «Flush the toilet» means to clean it by making water rush through it.
fact: «Flush» can mean to go red in the face, from heat, embarrassment or being upset.
fact: «Flush» as an adjective means exactly level with another surface.
fact: Close the lid before you flush, so germs do not spray out, and then wash your hands.
exercise: «When you flush, a valve opens and water rushes into the bowl.» What does flush mean here? | To be exactly level with something | To go red in the face | To make someone come out of hiding | *To clean something by making water rush through it
exercise: «Her face flushed when the whole class laughed.» What does flushed mean? | *To go red in the face from embarrassment | Level with the floor | To clean with water | Hidden away behind a door
exercise: The shelf sits «flush with the wall». What does flush mean here? | Hiding from view | Wet and dripping | Going red in the face | *Exactly level with the wall
test: «The hunters tried to flush the fox out of the bushes.» What does flush out mean here? | To make it go red | To make it fall asleep | To wash it with water | *To make it come out of hiding
test: Which of these is safe to flush down the toilet? | Cotton buds | Toys | *Toilet paper | Wipes
exam: Read: «The tiles are flush with the floor.» What is the best meaning of flush? | To go red in the face | *To be exactly level | To rush water into a bowl | To hide from someone
